763	Multi-head attention allows the model to jointly attend to information from different representation\nsubspaces at different positions. With a single attention head, averaging inhibits this.\n4To illustrate why the dot products get large, assume that the components of q and k are independent random\nvariables with mean 0 and variance 1.	{"type": "text", "page": 4, "source": "attention.pdf", "doc_sha256": "a0efa62491d3455cc071d16fb2cd6dc7172f2fa021b1bea951d78338c87d4d7f", "_node_content": "{\\"id_\\": \\"01729fe495072e6025714fdf6cbc4d1a1ebef2f86ed0dfdcb55a3ae279a65ab4\\", \\"embedding\\": null, \\"metadata\\": {\\"type\\": \\"text\\", \\"page\\": 4, \\"source\\": \\"attention.pdf\\", \\"doc_sha256\\": \\"a0efa62491d3455cc071d16fb2cd6dc7172f2fa021b1bea951d78338c87d4d7f\\"}, \\"excluded_embed_metadata_keys\\": [\\"type\\", \\"page\\", \\"source\\", \\"doc_sha256\\"], \\"excluded_llm_metadata_keys\\": [\\"type\\", \\"page\\", \\"source\\", \\"doc_sha256\\"], \\"relationships\\": {\\"1\\": {\\"node_id\\": \\"800befac-6182-4f55-a12f-5693205bcf0a\\", \\"node_type\\": \\"4\\", \\"metadata\\": {\\"type\\": \\"text\\", \\"page\\": 4, \\"source\\": \\"attention.pdf\\", \\"doc_sha256\\": \\"a0efa62491d3455cc071d16fb2cd6dc7172f2fa021b1bea951d78338c87d4d7f\\"}, \\"hash\\": \\"eab009da9432b713608ad527f70a8baf0b5f32b870f7b79dd7a5907e0d493e04\\", \\"class_name\\": \\"RelatedNodeInfo\\"}, \\"2\\": {\\"node_id\\": \\"440f5f8f-db28-41f5-9863-808c70e77a93\\", \\"node_type\\": \\"1\\", \\"metadata\\": {\\"type\\": \\"text\\", \\"page\\": 4, \\"source\\": \\"attention.pdf\\", \\"doc_sha256\\": \\"a0efa62491d3455cc071d16fb2cd6dc7172f2fa021b1bea951d78338c87d4d7f\\"}, \\"hash\\": \\"a3fa4b7938e27027b36c23b593b4335be916f61f38e1a14856f5dd413e59625c\\", \\"class_name\\": \\"RelatedNodeInfo\\"}, \\"3\\": {\\"node_id\\": \\"77e0fd4c-042c-4fdb-8b54-c6b15128a3a7\\", \\"node_type\\": \\"1\\", \\"metadata\\": {}, \\"hash\\": \\"fd01ba513af2b74e2c8ea8cb3afbc5ef4f25ad2b2507530a6cd169d614b9b4a3\\", 